Statements:
[
    "Retrieval‑Augmented Generation (RAG) combines a large‑language model (LLM) with a retrieval system that fetches relevant documents from an internal knowledge base.",
    "In customer support, RAG lets agents and bots answer questions using up‑to‑date, authoritative information while keeping the generative model lightweight.",
    "The text summarizes the most common real‑world deployments, the advantages they bring, and the challenges that remain.",
    "Live Agent Assistance: An agent queries RAG for purchase history, warranty data, or troubleshooting steps and embeds that context into the reply.",
    "Self‑service Chatbots: Bots retrieve current product specs, FAQ excerpts, or policy documents before generating an answer, allowing users to resolve issues without a human.",
    "Domain‑Specific Knowledge Bases: Internal documents (legal, financial, technical) are indexed in a vector store; the LLM uses those snippets to generate precise responses, cutting hallucinations.",
    "Rapid Knowledge Updates: New product releases or policy changes can be added to the retrieval index without retraining the LLM, speeding up deployment.",
    "Personalisation & Compliance: RAG pulls a user’s profile from an on‑premises system, enabling tailored answers while keeping data local to satisfy privacy regulations.",
    "Knowledge‑Graph‑Enhanced Assistance: Combining vector retrieval with a knowledge graph captures deeper semantic relationships across fragmented enterprise data.",
    "K2View, Thomson Reuters, and MDPI note that reducing hallucinations is a core advantage of RAG.",
    "K2View cites quicker time to value at lower cost because no expensive model retraining is required.",
    "Microsoft ties accurate, real‑time answers to enhancing the user experience and fostering trust, increasing customer loyalty.",
    "Thomson Reuters highlights the ability to cite the source of each answer.",
    "Meilisearch states RAG improves support accuracy and reduces ticket volume while keeping a single LLM.",
    "Microsoft and Dataworkz note that data can stay on‑premises, meeting residency and regulatory rules.",
    "Poor user phrasing can lead to irrelevant passages; the quality of the retriever and prompt engineering is critical.",
    "The additional retrieval step adds delay, especially at scale.",
    "Vector‑only retrieval may miss deep relationships; knowledge graphs can help bridge this.",
    "Token‑based pricing for embedding and generation can become expensive as usage grows.",
    "Handling sensitive customer data requires strict controls on the retrieval pipeline.",
    "Continuous ingestion, cleaning, and re‑indexing of enterprise documents is required.",
    "Most sources are vendor case studies or early‑stage papers; systematic, peer‑reviewed benchmarks are scarce.",
    "RAG is already deployed in live support calls, self‑service bots, and internal tools, and its core strength is pulling the right enterprise data before generating a response.",
    "Key advantages include factual correctness, cost‑effective updates, provenance, personalization, scalability, and compliance.",
    "Key hurdles include ensuring high‑quality retrieval for noisy queries, managing latency and token costs, maintaining a fresh, secure retrieval index, and addressing semantic gaps that simple vector search cannot fill.",
    "While vendor and early academic reports are promising, large‑scale, independent performance studies are still limited."
] 

